    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (79.71) stands as our premier offensive anchor, benefiting from a soft matchup against Montero. His elite projection is buoyed by favorable park factors and the stability of hitting second, making him a cornerstone for counting stats. **Will Smith** (65.60) and **Daulton Varsho** (63.66) round out our top-tier trio; while **Daulton Varsho** faces a moderate challenge in Warren, his dynamic platoon advantage and a wind-assisted environment provide the necessary lift to push him well into the \"Strong\" category. **Jung Hoo Lee** (62.55) and **Luis Arraez** (61.05) remain efficient, high-floor plays, with **Jung Hoo Lee** seeing a significant boost from his projected leadoff role against Ryne Nelson, a pitcher we are actively looking to exploit across our lineup today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Taylor Ward** (39.38), who narrowly missed the starting cut by failing to clear our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. Despite the positive outlook of a leadoff spot, his score was dragged down by an unfavorable matchup against Jax and significant regression in his platoon splits, forcing us to prioritize the higher-ceiling efficiency of **Gavin Sheets** (41.89) and **Drew Gilbert** (47.79). Meanwhile, we are monitoring the status of **Jonathan Aranda** (46.30) and **Bryson Stott** (53.36) closely; both face challenging opposing arms in Bradish and Burns, respectively. These matchups are riskier than they appear, and any late-breaking wind shifts at these ballparks could force us to reconsider our bench composition if we need to pinch-hit for contact or speed later in the evening.",
